+"""Client for the internal reports/exports API.
+
+``ApiClient`` is a thin, synchronous, GET-only wrapper. It builds requests,
+hands them to an injected ``Transport`` (see ``src.transport``), applies the
+retry rules below, and turns JSON bodies into the dataclasses in
+``src.models``. See README.md for the full integration guide.
+
+Requests
+    URL = ``config.base_url`` (trailing ``/`` stripped) + endpoint path. Path
+    IDs (``get_report``/``get_export``) are percent-encoded with no safe
+    characters, so ``/``, spaces etc. can't escape the path segment. Query
+    parameters whose value is ``None`` are dropped; the rest are encoded with
+    ``urllib.parse.quote`` (space -> ``%20``, ``&`` -> ``%26``, ``/`` ->
+    ``%2F``). Every request carries ``Accept: application/json``,
+    ``Authorization: Bearer <config.token>`` and ``User-Agent:
+    <config.user_agent>``. Each transport call gets
+    ``config.timeout_seconds`` as its timeout.
+
+Dates and times
+    Naive ``datetime`` values are treated as UTC (not machine-local time).
+    Aware values are converted. Microseconds are dropped.
+
+    * ``list_reports`` ``since``/``until``: converted to a fixed UTC-05:00
+      offset (``REPORTS_TZ``, "America/Bogota") and sent as local wall-clock
+      time with no offset, ``YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS``. ``until`` is exclusive.
+    * ``list_exports`` ``created_after``: sent as UTC,
+      ``YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ``.
+
+    Timestamps in responses (``Report.period_start``, ``Export.created_at``)
+    are returned as the raw strings the server sent; they are not parsed.
+
+Errors
+    Any final response with status >= 400 raises ``ApiError`` with ``status``,
+    ``path`` (endpoint path without base URL or query string) and the raw
+    ``body``. Exceptions raised by the transport (timeouts, connection errors)
+    are not caught or retried. A 2xx/3xx body that isn't valid JSON, or that
+    lacks the expected fields, raises the underlying ``ValueError``/``KeyError``.
+
+Retries (both loops call ``sleep``, which is injectable and defaults to
+``time.sleep``)
+    * HTTP 429, all endpoints: wait ``Retry-After`` seconds and resend, up to
+      ``config.rate_limit_retries`` (default 3) times. Only a non-negative
+      whole number of seconds is honored; a missing, fractional or HTTP-date
+      value waits 1 second. The value is not capped.
+    * HTTP 400, only the ``/v2/reports`` list endpoint (``FLAKY_ENDPOINTS``;
+      ``get_report`` is excluded): up to ``config.retry_attempts`` (default 5)
+      total attempts with linear backoff ``retry_backoff_seconds * n`` (0.5s,
+      1s, 1.5s, 2s by default). This also retries 400s caused by genuinely
+      bad input. Each attempt runs its own 429 loop, so the worst case is
+      ``retry_attempts * (rate_limit_retries + 1)`` sends.
+    * Nothing else is retried, including 5xx responses (even with
+      ``Retry-After``) and transport errors.
+"""
 
